2025-08-06 21:50:42 | INFO     | api.endpoints.qa:generate_sse:527 - [KNOWLEDGE_DEBUG] 收集到的具体团队知识来源: [{'id': 'e27a31a1-1747-41be-855f-197c1c7e5df9', 'content': '问题: 不同偏高岭土含量的 ghiara 基碱激活材料（GM1系列）的抗压强度随偏高岭土含量变化的趋势如何？\n答案: 不同偏高岭土含量的 ghiara 基碱激活材料（GM1系列）的抗压强度随偏高岭土含量变化的趋势如何？', 'title': 'QA: 不同偏高岭土含量的 ghiara 基碱激活材料（GM1系列）的抗压强度随偏高岭土含量变化的趋势如何？...', 'score': 0.48861431999999994, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_database', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'question': '不同偏高岭土含量的 ghiara 基碱激活材料（GM1系列）的抗压强度随偏高岭土含量变化的趋势如何？', 'answer': '不同偏高岭土含量的 ghiara 基碱激活材料（GM1系列）的抗压强度随偏高岭土含量变化的趋势如何？'}, {'id': '610f05f1-4499-424a-b673-cada4d57db1f', 'content': '问题: 比较H3和H4的28天抗压强度：H3为11.2 MPa，H4为9.3 MPa。H3的Ca/(Al+Si)原子比为0.48，而H4高达1.10。此外，H4含有大量的游离CaO（9.6%），远高于H3（3.5%）。请分析这些化学组成差异如何导致H4的强度低于H3。\n答案: A：H4的28天抗压强度（9.3 MPa）低于H3（11.2 MPa），尽管H4的Ca/(Al+Si)原子比（1.10）和总CaO含量（40.6%）远高于H3（0.48和26.2%）。这种反常现象主要是由于H4中过高的游离氧化钙含量（9.6%）导致。过量游离CaO的水化膨胀在材料内部产生破坏性应力，导致裂纹和剥落，从而抵消了高钙对强度发展的潜在益处。相比之下，H3的钙含量虽然也高，但游离CaO相对适中（3.5%），使得生成的(N,C)-A-S-H凝胶能有效发挥胶凝作用，形成更稳定的结构。', 'title': 'QA: 比较H3和H4的28天抗压强度：H3为11.2 MPa，H4为9.3 MPa。H3的Ca/(Al+S...', 'score': 0.48237131999999994, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_database', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'question': '比较H3和H4的28天抗压强度：H3为11.2 MPa，H4为9.3 MPa。H3的Ca/(Al+Si)原子比为0.48，而H4高达1.10。此外，H4含有大量的游离CaO（9.6%），远高于H3（3.5%）。请分析这些化学组成差异如何导致H4的强度低于H3。', 'answer': 'A：H4的28天抗压强度（9.3 MPa）低于H3（11.2 MPa），尽管H4的Ca/(Al+Si)原子比（1.10）和总CaO含量（40.6%）远高于H3（0.48和26.2%）。这种反常现象主要是由于H4中过高的游离氧化钙含量（9.6%）导致。过量游离CaO的水化膨胀在材料内部产生破坏性应力，导致裂纹和剥落，从而抵消了高钙对强度发展的潜在益处。相比之下，H3的钙含量虽然也高，但游离CaO相对适中（3.5%），使得生成的(N,C)-A-S-H凝胶能有效发挥胶凝作用，形成更稳定的结构。'}, {'id': '8d1ecd44-f00f-4c96-9f21-fad86be874e3', 'content': '问题: 对比经过100°C和400°C热处理的 ghiara 基碱激活材料，它们的无定形相丰度有何不同？这种差异说明了什么？\n答案: 对比经过100°C和400°C热处理的 ghiara 基碱激活材料，它们的无定形相丰度有何不同？这种差异说明了什么？', 'title': 'QA: 对比经过100°C和400°C热处理的 ghiara 基碱激活材料，它们的无定形相丰度有何不同？这种...', 'score': 0.46345706, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_database', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'question': '对比经过100°C和400°C热处理的 ghiara 基碱激活材料，它们的无定形相丰度有何不同？这种差异说明了什么？', 'answer': '对比经过100°C和400°C热处理的 ghiara 基碱激活材料，它们的无定形相丰度有何不同？这种差异说明了什么？'}, {'id': '2843ddd0-630f-41c8-8625-460d1748aadd', 'content': '问题: 与火山灰相比， ghiara 材料在化学组成上存在哪些主要差异？这些差异可能对其碱激活性能产生什么影响？\n答案: 与火山灰相比， ghiara 材料在化学组成上存在哪些主要差异？这些差异可能对其碱激活性能产生什么影响？', 'title': 'QA: 与火山灰相比， ghiara 材料在化学组成上存在哪些主要差异？这些差异可能对其碱激活性能产生什么影...', 'score': 0.4386302800000001, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_database', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'question': '与火山灰相比， ghiara 材料在化学组成上存在哪些主要差异？这些差异可能对其碱激活性能产生什么影响？', 'answer': '与火山灰相比， ghiara 材料在化学组成上存在哪些主要差异？这些差异可能对其碱激活性能产生什么影响？'}, {'id': '9ee42968-2e0f-4124-ab1d-3c8f422ee92d', 'content': '问题: 比较Hal450°C-10M和Hal750°C-10M在10 mol/L磷酸活化下，其SEM图像所示的微观结构差异及其对宏观性能的影响。\n答案: 比较Hal450°C-10M和Hal750°C-10M在10 mol/L磷酸活化下，其SEM图像所示的微观结构差异及其对宏观性能的影响。', 'title': 'QA: 比较Hal450°C-10M和Hal750°C-10M在10 mol/L磷酸活化下，其SEM图像所示...', 'score': 0.4217257000000001, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_database', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'question': '比较Hal450°C-10M和Hal750°C-10M在10 mol/L磷酸活化下，其SEM图像所示的微观结构差异及其对宏观性能的影响。', 'answer': '比较Hal450°C-10M和Hal750°C-10M在10 mol/L磷酸活化下，其SEM图像所示的微观结构差异及其对宏观性能的影响。'}, {'id': '94437524-4d1f-40ab-80d6-12eac7008b99', 'content': '\\pm 8$ hours and marked with respect to batch and mix id no, then immediately returned to the curing room. During the stripping time extra care was taken to avoid any type of damage of the specimens. The geopolymer and OPC concrete samples were put in different curing environment conditions. ![0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_543_303_605_460_0.jpg](images/0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_543_303_605_460_0.jpg)\n## Figure 3-5: Geopolymer concrete specimens cured at ambient condition.\nGeopolymer concrete samples were cured at ambient condition $\\left( {{15} - {20}^{0}\\mathrm{C}}\\right.$ and ${60} \\pm {10}\\% \\mathrm{{RH}}$ ) until the test days in the designated laboratory curing room.\nOrdinary Portland cement concrete specimens were cured under water up to 28 days and after that they were cured in the room environment $\\left( {{23}^{0}\\mathrm{C}}\\right.$ and ${60} \\pm {10}\\%$ RH) until test.\n![0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_528_1328_630_483_0.jpg](images/0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_528_1328_630_483_0.jpg)\nFigure 3-6: OPC concrete specimens cured in lime saturated water curing tank.\nCapping was done at 26 days in accordance with ASTM C-617 (ASTM standard, 2012b). Forney Hi-cap high strength capping compound was used for capping of the cylinders. If any defects were found in capping then cylinder was recapped before the testing.\n### 3.6. Test procedure\n#### 3.6.1. Particle size distribution.\nSieve analysis was used to determine the proportion of particles of different sizes within a particular aggregate product. The test used a tower of interlocking sieves with apertures that decreased in size from top to bottom. Sieve analysis was conducted as per the AS 1289.3.6.1-2009 (Standard Australia, 2009).\n## Fine aggregate\nThe test sample(1kg)was dried to a constant weight at a temperature of ${110} \\pm {5}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and weighed.', 'title': '', 'score': 0.24, 'source_type': 'document', 'source': 'knowledge_base', 'metadata': {'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'extra': None, 'headings': [], 'strategy': 'semantic', 'page_number': [1], 'dual_vector_metadata': "{'general_text': '\\\\pm 8$ hours and marked with respect to batch and mix id no, then immediately returned to the curing room. During the stripping time extra care was taken to avoid any type of damage of the specimens. The geopolymer and OPC concrete samples were put in different curing environment conditions. ![0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_543_303_605_460_0.jpg](images/0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_543_303_605_460_0.jpg)\\n## Figure 3-5: Geopolymer concrete specimens cured at ambient condition.\\nGeopolymer concrete samples were cured at ambient condition $\\\\left( {{15} - {20}^{0}\\\\mathrm{C}}\\\\right.$ and ${60} \\\\pm {10}\\\\% \\\\mathrm{{RH}}$ ) until the test days in the designated laboratory curing room.\\nOrdinary Portland cement concrete specimens were cured under water up to 28 days and after that they were cured in the room environment $\\\\left( {{23}^{0}\\\\mathrm{C}}\\\\right.$ and ${60} \\\\pm {10}\\\\%$ RH) until test.\\n![0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_528_1328_630_483_0.jpg](images/0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_528_1328_630_483_0.jpg)\\nFigure 3-6: OPC concrete specimens cured in lime saturated water curing tank.\\nCapping was done at 26 days in accordance with ASTM C-617 (ASTM standard, 2012b). Forney Hi-cap high strength capping compound was used for capping of the cylinders. If any defects were found in capping then cylinder was recapped before the testing.\\n### 3.6. Test procedure\\n#### 3.6.1. Particle size distribution.\\nSieve analysis was used to determine the proportion of particles of different sizes within a particular aggregate product. The test used a tower of interlocking sieves with apertures that decreased in size from top to bottom. Sieve analysis was conducted as per the AS 1289.3.6.1-2009 (Standard Australia, 2009).\\n## Fine aggregate\\nThe test sample(1kg)was dried to a constant weight at a temperature of ${110} \\\\pm {5}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}$ and weighed.', 'domain_text': '\\\\pm 8$ hours and marked with respect to batch and mix id no, then immediately returned to the curing room. During the stripping time extra care was taken to avoid any type of damage of the specimens. The geopolymer and OPC concrete samples were put in different curing environment conditions. ![0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_543_303_605_460_0.jpg](images/0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_543_303_605_460_0.jpg)\\n## Figure 3-5: Geopolymer concrete specimens cured at ambient condition.\\nGeopolymer concrete samples were cured at ambient condition $\\\\left( {{15} - {20}^{0}\\\\mathrm{C}}\\\\right.$ and ${60} \\\\pm {10}\\\\% \\\\mathrm{{RH}}$ ) until the test days in the designated laboratory curing room.\\nOrdinary Portland cement concrete specimens were cured under water up to 28 days and after that they were cured in the room environment $\\\\left( {{23}^{0}\\\\mathrm{C}}\\\\right.$ and ${60} \\\\pm {10}\\\\%$ RH) until test.\\n![0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_528_1328_630_483_0.jpg](images/0197448a-5ae2-7ee0-acc3-abe53a1a126a_53_528_1328_630_483_0.jpg)\\nFigure 3-6: OPC concrete specimens cured in lime saturated water curing tank.\\nCapping was done at 26 days in accordance with ASTM C-617 (ASTM standard, 2012b). Forney Hi-cap high strength capping compound was used for capping of the cylinders. If any defects were found in capping then cylinder was recapped before the testing.\\n### 3.6. Test procedure\\n#### 3.6.1. Partic', 'original_tokens': 557, 'general_tokens': 557, 'domain_tokens': 466, 'text_adapted': True, 'tokenizer_used': 'matbert_tokenizer_for_domain'}"}, 'highlights': {'content': ['Forney <mark>Hi</mark>-cap high strength capping compound was used for capping of the cylinders.']}}]
